[thin] The water-regulator cap's spring leaves and solid retaining nose define its fitted flexure and catch surfaces. Derek has physically approved that fitted section. The free point has its own lead-in above the retaining nose; thin readings at that taper's mathematical edge are inherent in the requested pointed profile. The point and flexible catch are required features, rather than bulk receiver walls.
alternatives: Increasing the spring thickness changes its accepted bending section. Blunting the nose removes the requested pointed lead-in. Increasing the retaining nose changes its fitted catch plane.
